 "早かれ遅かれ": "عَاجِلاً أَم آجِلاً, عَاجِلاً أَو آجِلاً (Eventually, at some undetermined time in the not-too-distant future.)  [sooner or later]",
 "早かろう悪かろう": "فِي الْعَجَلَة اَلنَّدَامَة, العجلة من الشيطان (Being too hasty leads to wasteful mistakes.)  [haste makes waste]",
 "早がわり": "[quick change (of costume)] / مَسْخ (A transformation, such as one performed by magic.) / مَسْخ (A change in the form and often habits of an animal after the embryonic stage dur)  [(sudden) metamorphosis]",
 "早く": "بَاكِر (At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.) / مُبَكِّرًا, بَاكِرًا (At a time before expected; sooner than usual.)  [early]\nمثال: それが君の生活をよくするのに役立つなら、いくら早くとりかかっても早すぎることはないよ。\n→ If it is useful for improving your life, it cannot be done too soon. / بِسُرْعَة, عَاجِلًا (Rapidly; with speed; fast; with expedition.)  [quickly]\nesp. 速く\nمثال: あなたが早くよくなるように祈っています。\n→ We are hoping for your quick recovery.",
 "早くも": "قَد, مِنْ قَبْلُ (Prior to some specified time, either past, present, or future; by this time; pre) / لقد (So soon.)  [already]\nمثال: まずいよ。また遅刻だ！！はやくも遅刻魔の異名をとってしまう。\n→ Oh no! I'm late again!! I'm going to get the nickname 'King of Late arrival'. / [at the earliest ; at the soonest]",
 "早さ": "سُرْعَة (The state of moving quickly or the capacity for rapid motion.) / سُرْعَة (The rate of motion or action, specifically the magnitude of the velocity; the ra)  [speed]\nesp. 速さ\nمثال: エイズウイルスの拡散は恐るべき速さで進んでいる。\n→ The speed of the spread of AIDS is horrifyingly fast. / [earliness]\nesp. 早さ",
 "早すぎる": "بَاكِر (At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.) / مُبَكِّرًا, بَاكِرًا (At a time before expected; sooner than usual.)  [early]",
 "早まる": "[to be brought forward (e.g. by three hours) ; to be moved up]\nمثال: 就職活動の時期は早まる傾向にあり、マスコミ各社の面接がその先頭にたっている。\n→ The job-seeking season is starting earlier each year and it's the mass media that are causing that trend by moving up their job interview… / [to be hasty ; to be rash]\nمثال: 早まって喜ぶな、最後に笑える者が勝ち。\n→ He laughs best who laughs last. / أَحْيَا (Senses relating to life or states of activity.) / سَرَّعَ (Senses relating to speed.)  [to quicken]\nesp. 速まる\nمثال: 心臓の鼓動が速まった。\n→ My heart quickened.",
 "早め": "بَاكِر (At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.) / مُبَكِّرًا, بَاكِرًا (At a time before expected; sooner than usual.)  [early]\nesp. 早め\nمثال: 早めの返事をお待ちしております。\n→ I look forward to hearing from you soon. / [a little faster than usual ; slightly quicker]\nesp. 速め",
 "早める": "يقرب (To move forward in space or time.)  [to advance]\nusu. 早める\nمثال: その薬が成長の過程を早めた。\n→ The medicine hastened the process of growth. / أَحْيَا (Senses relating to life or states of activity.) / سَرَّعَ (Senses relating to speed.)  [to quicken (e.g. one's step)]\nusu. 速める\nمثال: 我々はふだんより足を速めて歩いた。\n→ We walked more quickly than usual.",
