 "是": "عَدْل, إِنْصَاف (The state or characteristic of being just or fair.) / عَدْل, عَدَالَة (The ideal of fairness, impartiality, etc., especially with regard to the punishm) / عَدْل (Judgment and punishment of a party who has allegedly wronged another.) / عَدْل, عَدَالَة (The civil power dealing with law.)  [justice]",
 "是が非でも": "بِأَيِّ ثَمَنٍ (As an absolute imperative; sparing no effort or expense)  [at all costs]\nمثال: これは、お前の体躯、護衛能力を考慮した上でのプランなのだ。是が非でもやってもらう。\n→ This is a plan that takes into account your stature and your ability to guard. By all means do it for me.",
 "是とする": "صَدَّقَ, وَافَقَ (To officially sanction; to ratify; to confirm; to set as satisfactory.) / اِسْتَحَسَنَ, وَافَقَ (To regard as good; to commend; to be pleased with; to think well of.) / وَافَقَ (To show to be worthy; to demonstrate the merits of.)  [to approve (of)]",
 "是正": "تَصْحِيح (The act of correcting.)  [correction]\nمثال: 製造業に比べて大きく遅れをとっている非製造業における生産性向上、それも設備投資の活性化により内外価格差の是正と成長力を確保するというのがベストシナリオだ。\n→ The best way for adjusting the gap between the internal and the external price and securing economic growth is to promote the…",
 "是者": "مُقَامِر (One who plays at a game of chance, who gambles.) / مُغَامِر (One who takes significant risks.)  [gambler]",
 "是認": "قُبُول, قَبُول (An expression granting permission; an indication of agreement with a proposal; a)  [approval]",
 "是非": "بِالتَّأْكِيد (In a way which is certain; with certainty.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (Without doubt, surely.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (An emphatic affirmative answer; of course.)  [certainly]\nمثال: 「キャッチボールしようか」「よし、是非やろう」\n→ \"How about playing catch?\" \"Sure, why not?\" / مَحَاسِن وَمَسَاوِئ (The advantages and disadvantages or positives and negatives regarding a specific)  [pros and cons]",
 "是非とも": "بِأَيِّ ثَمَنٍ (As an absolute imperative; sparing no effort or expense)  [at all costs]\nمثال: あなたの迅速な返事が是非とも必要です。\n→ Your prompt reply is urgently required.",
 "是非ない": "وَاجِب (Impossible to avoid; bound to happen.)  [unavoidable]",
