 "時を同じくして": "فِي نَفْس اَلْوَقْت (Overlapping or coinciding in duration.)  [at the same time]",
 "時を移さず": "حَالاً (Immediately; now; right away.)  [at once]\nمثال: 時を移さず救急車がやってきた。\n→ An ambulance arrived immediately.",
 "時下": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now]\nusu. at the beginning of letters",
 "時世": "فِي (Multiplied by (see also 'ratio of comparison' sense at 'time').)  [the times]\nمثال: 彼女は時世が悪いのだと言った。\n→ She cursed the times.",
 "時人": "مُعَاصِر (From the same time period, coexistent in time; contemporaneous.) / عَصْرِيّّ, حَدِيث (Modern, of the present age (shorthand for ‘contemporary with the present’).)  [contemporaries]",
 "時代": "نُقْطَة, عَلَامَة فَصْلِيَّة (The punctuation mark “.” (indicating the ending of a sentence or marking an abbr) / حِصَّةٌ (Each of the divisions into which a school day is split, allocated to a given sub) / عَصْر (A geochronologic unit of millions to tens of millions of years; a subdivision of)  [period]\nمثال: 今や時代との競争になった。\n→ It was now a race against time. / فِي (Multiplied by (see also 'ratio of comparison' sense at 'time').)  [the times] / تَارِيخ قَدِيم (ancient times)  [antiquity] / عَتِيق, قَدِيم (Belonging to former times, not modern, out of date, old-fashioned.)  [antique]",
 "時代物": "عَتِيق, قَدِيم (Belonging to former times, not modern, out of date, old-fashioned.)  [antique] / [pre-Meiji period drama ; period piece]",
 "時代精神": "رُوحُ الْعَصْر (The spirit of the age; the taste, outlook, and spirit characteristic of a period)  [zeitgeist]",
 "時代遅れ": "عَتِيق, بَالٍ (old-fashioned, out of date)  [antiquated]\nمثال: あなたの考えはまったく時代遅れである。\n→ Your ideas are all out of date.",
