 "本場": "وَطَن (One’s native land; the place or country in which one dwells; the place where one)  [home (of something)] / مَكَان الْمِيلَاد, مَسْقَط الرَّأْس (The location where a person or an animal was born.)  [birthplace]\nمثال: 日本にあるインドカレー屋のカレーって、やっぱり日本人の口に合わせて本場よりマイルドに作られてるよね。\n→ The curry they serve in Japan is milder than real Indian curry. They adapt it to Japanese tastes. / [morning session ; last session in the morning]",
 "本塁": "قَاعِدَة (A site, structure, or both, usually durable and often permanent, for housing mil) / قَاعِدَة, مَرْكَز (The place where decisions for an organization are made; headquarters.) / قَاعِدَة (The lowest side of a triangle or other polygon, or the lowest face of a cone, py) / يُبْنَى عَلَى, يَسْتَنِدُ إِلَى (To give as its foundation or starting point; to lay the foundation of.) / شائع (Of low social standing or rank; vulgar, common.) / منخفض, فاسق (Morally reprehensible, immoral; cowardly.) / دنيء (Inferior; unworthy, of poor quality.)  [base] / [home base ; home plate]",
