 "根付く": "جَذْر, جدر (The part of a plant, generally underground, that anchors and supports the plant ) / جَذْر (The part of a tooth extending into the bone holding the tooth in place.) / أَصْل (The primary source; origin.) / جَذْر (Of a number or expression, a number which, when raised to a specified power, yie) / جَذْر (The primary lexical unit of a word, which carries the most significant aspects o) / أَصْل (A word from which another word or words are derived.)  [to root]\nمثال: 実も結ぶが、挿し木でも根付くらしい？\n→ It bears fruit, but it seems it may even set root from cuttings? / [to become established (e.g. of an idea, a movement) ; to take hold]\nمثال: 西洋の多くの習慣が日本に根付いてきた。\n→ Many western customs have taken root in Japan.",
