 "止める": "وَقَفَ, تَوَقَّفَ (To cease moving.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to cease moving or progressing.) / تَوَقَّفَ, وَقَّف (To cease; to no longer continue.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to come to an end.) / مَوْقِف (A (usually marked) place where buses, trams or trains halt to let passengers get) / وَقْفَة (An action of stopping; interruption of travel.)  [to stop]\nesp. 止める, 停める\nمثال: その新聞は政府にインフレを止めるように求めた。\n→ The newspaper called for the government to stop inflation. / حَدِيقَة (An area of land set aside for environment preservation or recreation.) / وَقَّفَ, صَفَّ (To bring (something such as a vehicle) to a halt or store in a specified place.)  [to park]\nesp. 止める, 停める\nمثال: ここに車を停めるのは違法です。\n→ It's illegal to park your car here. / مَنَعَ (To stop (an outcome); to keep from (doing something).)  [to prevent]\nesp. 止める, 停める / وَقَفَ, تَوَقَّفَ (To cease moving.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to cease moving or progressing.) / تَوَقَّفَ, وَقَّف (To cease; to no longer continue.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to come to an end.) / مَوْقِف (A (usually marked) place where buses, trams or trains halt to let passengers get) / وَقْفَة (An action of stopping; interruption of travel.)  [to stop (someone from doing something)]\nمثال: この文書はあなたのお目にだけ留めていただきたい。\n→ This document is for your eyes only.",
