 "正": "حَقٌّ (Loyal, faithful.)  [(logical) true] / [10^40 ; ten duodecillion] / أَصْلِيّ (First in a series of copies or versions.)  [original] / مُوجَب (Greater than zero.) / إِيجَابِيّ (Actual, real, concrete, not theoretical or speculative.) / مُوجَب (Having more protons than electrons.) / صُورَة مُوجَبَة (A positive image; one that displays true colors and shades, not their opposites )  [positive]",
 "正々": "مَضْبُوط (exact or careful conformity to truth) / دَقِيق (exact or careful conformity to truth)  [accurate]",
 "正しい": "يَمِين, يمين (Clockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation.) / صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Complying with justice, correctness, or reason; correct, just, true. See also th) / قَائِم (Of an angle, measuring 90 degrees, or one quarter of a complete rotation; the an) / عَلَى اَلْيَمِين (On the right side.) / إِلَى اَلْيَمِين (Towards the right side.) / صحيح, تمام (Yes, that is correct; I agree.) / حَقّ, حُقُوق (A legal, just or moral entitlement.) / يَمِين (A wave breaking from right to left (viewed from the shore).) / صَحَّحَ (To correct.)  [right]\nمثال: これが正しいかどうか自信がないんだ。\n→ I'm not sure if this is correct. / صَالِح (Free from sin or guilt.) / صَالِح (Moral and virtuous, perhaps to the point of sanctimony.) / صَالِح (Justified morally.)  [righteous]",
 "正しく": "بِالتَّأْكِيد (In a way which is certain; with certainty.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (Without doubt, surely.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (An emphatic affirmative answer; of course.)  [certainly]\nمثال: 彼女はまさしく支払わされたのだ。\n→ She was jolly well made to pay. / عَدْل (Morally right; upright, righteous, equitable; fair.) / فَقَط (only, simply, merely)  [just]",
 "正す": "صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Free from error; true; accurate.) / صَحَّحَ (To make something that was wrong become right; to remove error from.)  [to correct]\nمثال: 間違いがあれば正しなさい。\n→ Correct errors, if any. / اِسْتَقَامَ (To become straight.)  [to straighten (one's posture, collar, etc.)]",
 "正に": "بِالضَّبْط, تَمَامًا (Without approximation; precisely.) / بِالْضَبْط (Signifies agreement or recognition.)  [exactly]\nمثال: ＤＴＰで本を作れば、安いし早いし、まさに一挙両得だ。\n→ Desktop publishing lets you produce books quickly and cheaply. It's like killing two birds with one stone. / يَمِين, يمين (Clockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation.) / صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Complying with justice, correctness, or reason; correct, just, true. See also th) / قَائِم (Of an angle, measuring 90 degrees, or one quarter of a complete rotation; the an) / عَلَى اَلْيَمِين (On the right side.) / إِلَى اَلْيَمِين (Towards the right side.) / صحيح, تمام (Yes, that is correct; I agree.) / حَقّ, حُقُوق (A legal, just or moral entitlement.) / يَمِين (A wave breaking from right to left (viewed from the shore).) / صَحَّحَ (To correct.)  [right (when)]\nمثال: あなたの電話が鳴ったときまさに出かけようとするところだった。\n→ I was about to leave when you telephoned. / عَدْل (Morally right; upright, righteous, equitable; fair.) / فَقَط (only, simply, merely)  [just (about to)]\nalso written as 将に / حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really (ought to)]\nas まさに...べき; also written as 当に",
 "正の数": "عَدَد مُوجَب  [positive number]",
 "正中": "مُنْتَصَف, وَسَط (A centre, midpoint.) / وَسَط, مُتَوَسْط (Located in the middle; in between.)  [middle] / نَزَاهَة, حِيَاد (The quality of being impartial; fairness.)  [impartiality] / [culmination]",
