 "毒する": "مُرْتَشٍ, فَاسِد (In a depraved state; debased; perverted; morally degenerate; weak in morals.) / أَفْسَدَ (To make corrupt; to change from good to bad; to draw away from the right path; t)  [to corrupt]\nمثال: そういえば。やばい、秀樹に毒されてるわ。\n→ Now that you mention it. Yeek, Hideki's habits are rubbing off on me!",
 "毒づく": "لَعْنَة (A supernatural detriment or hindrance; a bane.) / لَعْنَة (A prayer or imprecation that harm may befall someone.) / نِقْمَة (The cause of great harm, evil, or misfortune; that which brings evil or severe a) / لَعَنَ (To place a curse upon (a person or object).) / لَعَنَ (To call upon divine or supernatural power to send injury upon; to imprecate evil) / شَتَمَ, سَبَّ (To use offensive or morally inappropriate language.)  [to curse (at someone)]\nمثال: 泥棒が見つかって警官に毒づいた。\n→ The thief cursed the police for finding him.",
 "毒のある": "سَامّ (Containing sufficient poison to be dangerous to touch or ingest.)  [poisonous] / [malicious ; spiteful]",
 "毒を盛る": "سُمّ, سَمّ (A substance that is harmful or lethal to a living organism when ingested.) / سَمَّمَ, سَمَّ (To use poison to kill or paralyse (somebody).)  [to poison (e.g. food, drink)]",
